What this does:

- Reduces the built-in fallback ratio from 0.50 (50% of original size) down to 0.25 (a more typical CSS gzip ratio of ~75% compression).
- When there is no network record (e.g. for inlined or dynamically injected styles), the audit will now estimate a smaller “transferred” size, which aligns better with real‐world CSS compression and eliminates the huge overestimates you saw (~80 KB).
